# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EVERYTHING HERE IS OPTIONAL.
#
# With this file empty the app runs in local-only mode: localStorage
# persistence, no sign-in, no AI, no live market data — exactly the behaviour
# it had before any of these were added. Fill in one line when you want that
# one feature; nothing depends on anything else here.
#
# Copy to .env.local (git-ignored) and edit.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# --- Cross-device sync -----------------------------------------------------
# Blank -> local-only mode, no login screen. See the README for setup.
# VITE_ vars are compiled into the browser bundle, so only put public keys here.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=


# --- AI features -----------------------------------------------------------
# Server-side only — deliberately NOT prefixed VITE_, so these never reach the
# browser bundle.
#
# Any OpenAI-compatible gateway works. Defaults target 9Router running locally.
# Get the key from the 9Router dashboard; its /v1/models endpoint is open but
# chat completions require one.
LLM_API_KEY=
LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:20128/v1

# NOTE: model availability on 9Router depends on your provider quotas, and
# they run out. The ag/* (antigravity) tiers -- Claude AND gemini -- all hit an
# "Individual quota reached" wall that resets on a ~7 day timer, and a single
# large batch job is enough to exhaust one. ollama/* runs locally, so it has no
# quota and is the safe default for long content runs. Check availability with:
#   curl -s localhost:20128/v1/models | python3 -m json.tool | grep '"id"'
# Thinking models spend part of max_tokens on reasoning before emitting any
# content, so the client keeps generous headroom.

# Cheap + fast: answer grading, follow-up questions, hints.
LLM_MODEL_FAST=ollama/gpt-oss:120b
# Stronger: question generation, market explanations, batch content scripts.
LLM_MODEL_SMART=ollama/gpt-oss:120b

# HEADS UP — a Vercel function cannot reach a gateway on your laptop, so with
# LLM_BASE_URL on localhost the live AI features are LOCAL-ONLY BY DESIGN:
# they work in `npm run dev` and in the batch scripts, and the deployed site
# hides them rather than showing buttons that fail.
#
# That loses very little. The expensive AI work is offline — cleaning the
# flashcard deck, generating the quant bank and the Learn modules — and those
# scripts commit their output, so the deployed app ships all that content at
# zero runtime cost.
#
# The two vars below are ONLY needed if you later decide you want live AI in
# production too. That would mean pointing LLM_BASE_URL at a hosted gateway
# (e.g. https://openrouter.ai/api/v1) and setting its key in Vercel; /api/ai
# then uses these to verify the caller before spending tokens. Leave blank
# otherwise — with no LLM_API_KEY in Vercel the route simply reports
# "not configured" and never runs.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=


# --- Live market data (Phase 5 — not used yet) ------------------------------
# https://finnhub.io/register — free tier, ~60 req/min
FINNHUB_API_KEY=
# https://fredaccount.stlouisfed.org/apikeys — free
FRED_API_KEY=
